messages.content:
{
  "message": "Great—thanks for the status details. Your data is refueled, so once we switch your phone to use faster networks and enable data/roaming, you should get online right away. Let’s do this step-by-step.",
  "thought_process": "Right now you’re on 2G with poor signal, and both Mobile Data and Data Roaming are OFF—this will either block data entirely or make it extremely slow. We’ll (1) turn Mobile Data ON, (2) enable Data Roaming for France, (3) force the phone to prefer 4G/5G, then (4) verify the new status and (5) speed test. If it still clings to 2G, we’ll refresh the radio and try a more targeted network mode.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "goal": "Enable data and roaming",
      "do": [
        "Run toggle_data to turn Mobile Data ON.",
        "Run toggle_roaming to turn Data Roaming ON."
      ],
      "why": "Mobile Data must be ON to use cellular internet; Data Roaming must be ON when abroad."
    },
    {
      "goal": "Prefer the fastest networks",
      "do": [
        "Run set_network_mode_preference with mode: \"4g_5g_preferred\"."
      ],
      "why": "2G is too slow for your needs. Preferring 4G/5G targets much higher speeds."
    },
    {
      "goal": "Verify the change",
      "do": [
        "Run check_network_status and share the results (signal strength and network type)."
      ],
      "expect": "Ideally you’ll now see 4G or 5G with at least fair/good signal."
    },
    {
      "goal": "Eliminate common speed limiters",
      "do": [
        "Run check_data_restriction_status; if Data Saver is ON, run toggle_data_saver_mode to turn it OFF.",
        "Run check_vpn_status; if a VPN is connected, run disconnect_vpn."
      ],
      "why": "Data Saver and VPNs can throttle or block traffic."
    },
    {
      "goal": "Measure performance",
      "do": [
        "With Wi‑Fi OFF, run run_speed_test and share the rating (very poor/poor/fair/good/excellent). We’re aiming for 'excellent'."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "if_still_on_2g_or_poor_signal": [
    "Quick radio refresh: run toggle_airplane_mode to turn it ON, wait 5–10 seconds, then run toggle_airplane_mode again to turn it OFF. Re-run check_network_status.",
    "If it still shows 2G, try set_network_mode_preference with mode: \"4g_only\" and check again. If you lose service entirely on 4g_only, switch back to \"4g_5g_preferred\".",
    "If data still won’t move past 2G, we’ll check carrier settings: run check_apn_settings and share the APN name and whether MMSC is set. If it looks wrong/missing, run reset_apn_settings, then run reboot_device to apply changes, and check again."
  ],
  "next": "Please do Steps 1–3 now and paste the new check_network_status results. Then proceed with Steps 4–5 and share the speed test rating so I can fine‑tune further if needed."
}

