messages.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for the update. You’ve got strong 5G signal and roaming + data are enabled, so the next most common blockers for MMS while roaming are Wi‑Fi Calling interference and APN/MMSC settings. We’ll check those first, then a couple of quick device settings.",
  "why_these_steps": [
    "Some networks don’t carry MMS over Wi‑Fi Calling; turning it off forces MMS over mobile data.",
    "MMS depends on the APN’s MMSC URL. If it’s missing/incorrect, MMS will spin and never send.",
    "Data Saver/VPN/app permissions can also block MMS from using data or accessing media."
  ],
  "step_by_step": [
    {
      "step": "Turn OFF Wi‑Fi Calling and keep Wi‑Fi OFF for testing",
      "how": "Android > Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile Network > Wi‑Fi Calling > OFF. Also confirm Wi‑Fi is OFF.",
      "reason": "Avoids MMS over Wi‑Fi paths that some carriers don’t support."
    },
    {
      "step": "Check APN and MMSC",
      "how": "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile Network > Access Point Names (APN) > tap your carrier APN > find the MMSC field.",
      "what_to_look_for": "MMSC must be filled with a URL (e.g., starts with http). If it’s blank or looks wrong:",
      "fix_if_wrong": "In the APN screen menu, tap “Reset to default” (or “Reset APNs”). After resetting, RESTART the phone.",
      "reason": "Incorrect or missing MMSC prevents MMS from sending."
    },
    {
      "step": "Try a test MMS to yourself",
      "how": "After confirming Wi‑Fi Calling is OFF and APN looks correct (or after the reboot if you reset APN), send one picture to your own number.",
      "reason": "Quick validation that MMS can traverse mobile data now."
    },
    {
      "step": "If still stuck, check these quick settings",
      "checks": [
        "Data Saver: Settings > Network & Internet > Data Saver > OFF.",
        "VPN: Settings > Network & Internet > VPN > Disconnect any active VPN.",
        "Messaging app permissions: Settings > Apps > Messaging (your SMS/MMS app) > Permissions > ensure “SMS” and “Storage/Photos and media” are ALLOWED."
      ],
      "reason": "These can silently block MMS from using data or media."
    },
    {
      "step": "Network mode (just to confirm)",
      "how": "Settings > Mobile Network > Preferred network type > 4G/5G preferred.",
      "reason": "You see 5G already, but confirming avoids a fallback to 2G/3G."
    }
  ],
  "what_to_report_back": [
    "Is Wi‑Fi Calling now OFF, and is Wi‑Fi OFF during testing?",
    "In the APN details, was the MMSC field present and populated? If you reset APN, did you reboot?",
    "Result of the test MMS to yourself (did it send?).",
    "If it still fails: confirm whether Data Saver is OFF, VPN is disconnected, and the messaging app has SMS + Storage permissions."
  ],
  "next_steps": "Please work through steps 1–3 first. If the test still fails, do step 4 (Data Saver/VPN/permissions) and try again. Share the results and I’ll guide you through the next targeted fix immediately."
}

