{
  "summary": "I found your line and everything on our side looks good. Since you’re in France, MMS likely isn’t sending because mobile data or data roaming is OFF on the phone, Wi‑Fi Calling/VPN is interfering, or the APN (MMSC) settings need a quick reset. We’ll run a few quick checks on your phone to fix it.",
  "what_i_checked_on_our_side": {
    "line": "555-123-2002",
    "status": "Active",
    "roaming_on_line": true,
    "plan": "Premium Plan (15 GB)",
    "data_used_this_cycle_gb": 8.7,
    "data_remaining_gb": 6.3,
    "billing_cycle_ends": "2025-02-28"
  },
  "what_this_means": "Your account and data allowance are fine, and roaming is enabled on your line. MMS relies on mobile data even if Wi‑Fi is on, so we’ll make sure your phone itself has mobile data and data roaming turned ON, and then check a couple of settings that commonly block MMS while abroad.",
  "first_small_help": {
    "how_to_tell_if_iphone_or_android": [
      "Open Settings > About (or About Phone). If you see 'iOS Version' or the name starts with 'iPhone', it’s an iPhone.",
      "If you see 'Android version' or a brand like Samsung/Google/OnePlus with 'Android', it’s an Android."
    ]
  },
  "steps_on_your_phone": [
    {
      "step": "Turn off Wi‑Fi just for testing",
      "why": "MMS must use mobile data. Turning off Wi‑Fi ensures the phone actually uses mobile data.",
      "how": [
        "Open Settings and turn Wi‑Fi OFF.",
        "Look at the top status bar: do you see 4G/LTE/5G (and possibly an R for roaming)?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Make sure Airplane Mode is OFF and Mobile Data is ON",
      "why": "If Airplane Mode is on or mobile data is off, MMS will fail.",
      "iphone": [
        "Settings > Airplane Mode: OFF",
        "Settings > Cellular (or Mobile Data) > Cellular Data: ON"
      ],
      "android": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections)",
        "Airplane mode: OFF",
        "Mobile data: ON"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Enable Data Roaming on the phone (you’re in France)",
      "why": "Even though your line is allowed to roam, the phone must also allow data roaming.",
      "iphone": [
        "Settings > Cellular > Cellular Data Options > Data Roaming: ON"
      ],
      "android": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Data roaming: ON"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Quick data test",
      "why": "Confirms mobile data works. If it doesn’t, MMS won’t work.",
      "how": [
        "With Wi‑Fi OFF and Mobile Data ON, open your browser and try loading example.com.",
        "Tell me if it loads normally, loads very slowly, or doesn’t load at all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Try sending a small MMS to yourself",
      "why": "This isolates the issue to your phone/settings (not the recipient).",
      "how": [
        "Send a photo to your own number and tell me what happens (still spinning/failing, or sent)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "If it still fails: temporarily turn OFF Wi‑Fi Calling",
      "why": "Some networks don’t handle MMS over Wi‑Fi Calling while roaming.",
      "iphone": [
        "Settings > Cellular > Wi‑Fi Calling: OFF (temporarily)"
      ],
      "android": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Wi‑Fi Calling: OFF (temporarily)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "If it still fails: check and reset APN settings (MMSC)",
      "why": "Incorrect or missing MMSC in the APN will block MMS.",
      "how_general": [
        "Open Settings > Cellular/Mobile Network > Access Point Names (APN).",
        "If you don’t know what’s correct, use the option to Reset/Restore APN to default.",
        "After resetting APN, restart the phone completely (power off, wait 10 seconds, power on).",
        "Try sending the MMS again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Optional checks if still stuck",
      "why": "These can also interfere with MMS/data while roaming.",
      "checks": [
        "VPN: If you use a VPN, turn it OFF and try again.",
        "Android only – Network mode: Settings > Mobile network > Preferred network type: set to 4G/5G (not 2G/3G)."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "my_thought_process": "Because your line is active with data remaining and roaming enabled, the most likely causes are phone-side: mobile data or data roaming toggles, Wi‑Fi Calling/VPN interference, or APN (MMSC) misconfiguration. We’re testing connectivity first, then eliminating common blockers, and finally resetting APN and rebooting so MMS can register correctly on the roaming network.",
  "questions_for_you": [
    "After Step 2 and 3, do you see 4G/LTE/5G (maybe an R) in the status bar?",
    "With Wi‑Fi OFF, does example.com load?",
    "After trying to send a photo to yourself, does it send or still fail?",
    "Is your phone an iPhone or Android (from the About screen)?"
  ],
  "next": "Please work through the steps until it either works or you hit a point you’re unsure about, then tell me exactly what you see. I’ll adjust the guidance based on your results."

