  "short_answer": "Yes—that airplane icon means Airplane Mode is ON, which turns off cellular service and will stop MMS from working. Let’s turn it OFF first.",
  "why": "Airplane Mode disables the cellular connection that MMS needs. Once we turn it off, your phone should reconnect to a local network in France.",
  "step_1_turn_off_airplane_mode": {
    "iphone": [
      "Open Control Center: swipe down from the top‑right (Face ID models) or swipe up from the bottom (Home button models).",
      "Tap the airplane icon so it is NOT highlighted (it should turn gray).",
      "Alternatively: Settings > Airplane Mode: turn it OFF."
    ],
    "android": [
      "Swipe down from the very top to open Quick Settings (swipe down twice if needed).",
      "Tap the airplane icon so it turns gray/off.",
      "Alternatively: Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Airplane mode: OFF."
    ],
    "after_toggling": [
      "Wait up to 30–60 seconds.",
      "Watch the top bar for signal bars and a label like 4G/LTE/5G. You might also see an “R” for roaming or a French carrier name."
    ]
  },
  "next_small_step": {
    "what_to_check": [
      "Do you now see signal bars?",
      "Do you see 4G/LTE/5G (and possibly an R for roaming)?"
    ],
    "then": "If you see those, we’ll quickly confirm Wi‑Fi is OFF just for testing and try a tiny web check."
  },
  "what_to_reply_with": [
    "Did the airplane icon disappear (Airplane Mode OFF)?",
    "Exactly what do you see in the top bar now (e.g., 4G/LTE/5G, an ‘R’, carrier name, or ‘No Service’)?"
  ],
  "my_thought_process": "Your line is active with roaming enabled and has data left. The airplane icon explains why MMS failed. Once we restore cellular service, we’ll verify mobile data/roaming toggles and do a quick test."
}

messages.content:
{
  "reassurance": "You did great turning Airplane Mode off. Since it now says “No Signal” and “Data Disabled,” we’ll take tiny steps to restore a cellular connection first, then enable data so MMS can work.",
  "why_this_step": "Right after switching off Airplane Mode, phones sometimes need a short moment to re-register on the local network. Then we’ll turn Mobile Data and Data Roaming ON so MMS can use data in France.",
  "steps_now": [
    {
      "step": "Let the phone reconnect",
      "how": [
        "Wait about 60–90 seconds and, if possible, move closer to a window or outdoors.",
        "Watch the top bar for any change from “No Signal” to bars or a carrier name."
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": "Turn ON Mobile Data",
      "iphone": [
        "Open Settings > Cellular (or Mobile Data).",
        "Turn Cellular Data ON."
      ],
      "android": [
        "Open Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network.",
        "Turn Mobile data ON."
      ],
      "why": "This will change “Data Disabled” to enabled so MMS can use mobile data."
    },
    {
      "step": "Enable Data Roaming (you’re in France)",
      "iphone": [
        "Settings > Cellular > Cellular Data Options > Data Roaming: ON."
      ],
      "android": [
        "Settings > Network & Internet (or Connections) > Mobile network > Data roaming: ON."
      ],
      "why": "Even though your line is allowed to roam on our side, your phone also needs roaming enabled to use data abroad."
    },
    {
      "step": "Check the top bar again",
      "what_to_look_for": [
        "Signal bars and a label like 4G/LTE/5G (you might also see an “R” for roaming).",
        "Confirm that “Data Disabled” is gone.",
        "Make sure there’s no airplane icon."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "if_still_no_signal_after_2_minutes": {
    "next_checks": [
      {
        "check": "SIM status",
        "iphone": [
          "Settings > Cellular: see if it shows your carrier or if it says No SIM.",
          "If you can’t tell, go to Settings > General > About and look for Network/Carrier info."
        ],
        "android": [
          "Settings > About phone > SIM status (or Status) > look for Network and Signal strength.",
          "If it says No service or No SIM, we may need to reseat the SIM."
        ],
        "why": "If the SIM isn’t detected or is locked, the phone can’t connect to any network."
      },
      {
        "action_if_sim_missing_or_no_service": "We can try reseating the SIM (safe and reversible). I’ll guide you step by step if needed."
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_reply_with": [
    "After waiting ~1 minute and turning Mobile Data and Data Roaming ON: what exactly do you see at the top now?",
    "Is “Data Disabled” gone?",
    "Do you see any bars and 4G/LTE/5G (maybe an R), or does it still say “No Signal”?"
  ],
  "my_thought_process": "Your account is active with roaming enabled and data remaining. The phone currently isn’t connected to a cellular network (hence No Signal) and has data switched off. Restoring network registration, then enabling data and data roaming are the most direct fixes for MMS abroad."
}

